44-save-and-load: curry.save and curry.load of a module and of a program on
the Python backend.

Seam: curry.save with module_main=False, with goal='main', without either,
and with a symbol as the goal; curry.save without a file name; curry.load
after a reset; the saved program run by the Python of the installation.
The run script copies go.py and M.curry into a temporary directory.
Sources: memo A16; catalogue P31, P39; example 04; Using the API,
"Writing Compiled Code to Disk".
Backends: py.  curry.load reads .so files alone on the C++ backend, and
the form of a saved program there is the open decision of #82 stage 5
(P31).  Oracle: none.

Expected output: M.f is 42; the two saved files are M.py and Prog.py; save
without a goal is a ValueError and goal=M.main a TypeError (P39); the text
of the module starts with "# SECTION: .header"; after the reset load gives
the module M with f 42, registered in curry.modules, and a second load
returns the same object.  The saved program prints [42, 43], the values
of main.  Pins no defect.
